  "body": "Found while fixing #91. Verify's rapid law (d) (`crates/sim/src/verify/rapids.rs`, the `dx*dx + dy*dy <= z_tol^2` arm) skips EVERY vertical rapid as \"a retract through the tool's own kerf\" - including rapids going DOWN into uncut stock. #91 closes the drilling case at generation (an R plane below the stock top is refused by name), but the law itself still lets any other op's vertical rapid into declared stock post silently.\n\nProof from the existing suites, with the held verify patch below applied (a downward vertical rapid whose `to.z` is below `Rest::surface_before` at its column, inside the stock, is `RapidInStock`):\n\n- `crates/app/tests/posting.rs` `contour_and_drill`: box stock 100x100x10 (top Z 10), Contour1 with clearance 10 / retract 8 over a 5 mm part - move 1 is a rapid 10 -> 8, 2 mm into the declared stock. Today it posts silently; with the patch, 6 posting tests fail on `RapidInStock { at: 1 }`.\n- `crates/app/tests/operations.rs` `the_shell_switch_sends_the_pocket_to_the_offset_engine`: box stock 60x60x20 (top Z 20), Pocket3D clearance 10 - move 1 rapids down inside the stock. Fails with `RapidInStock { at: 1 }` under the patch.\n\nBoth fixtures are real collisions by their own declared stock (the tool rapids below the stock top), so the fix is the law plus fixture repairs; the blast radius over the rest of the app/ui suites and the .nc goldens is unmeasured - which is why it was held out of #91.\n\nHeld patch (sim, 10 lines; peck re-entries above their own earlier plunge stay clean because the cut-order chords acquit them):\n\n```diff\n             if dx * dx + dy * dy <= cx.z_tol * cx.z_tol {\n-                continue; // vertical retract through the tool's own kerf\n+                let down = m.to.z < m.from.z - cx.z_tol;\n+                if down && rest.in_stock(a) && m.to.z < rest.surface_before(a, i) - cx.z_tol {\n+                    warns.push(Warning::RapidInStock { at: i });\n+                }\n+                continue;\n             }\n```\n\nA verify-level test file was written for it (4 tests: R plane under stock top convicts; R over the stock top is clean; peck re-entry above its plunge clean; re-entry past its plunge convicts) - all green with the patch, `cargo test -p camcraft-sim` otherwise unchanged (all green).\n\nDone means: the law lands, every suite that trips it is checked fixture-by-fixture (real collision -> fix the fixture; a false conviction -> fix the law), goldens re-verified.\n",
